{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && printf '\\\\n--- AGENTS ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && printf '\\\\n--- STATUS ---\\\\n' && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n\n--- AGENTS ---\n# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n\n--- STATUS ---\n M AGENTS.md\n M Formalization.lean\n M PROGRESS.md\n M README.md\n M aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/BicommutantNormalTransport.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarAlphaGNSBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarCompletionAlphaInterface.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarGNSBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ConcreteCStarCompletion.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ConstructedAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarEquiv.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateEquivCoherence.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateFactorization.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteProductStateCoherence.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteStabilizerProductState.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/InfiniteAlgebraicRegionalEquiv.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/InfiniteAlgebraicStateTransport.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalVonNeumannExtensionInterface.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/ProductFactorClassificationBoundary.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StatePreservingGNSModel.lean\n?? Formalization/Infrastructure.lean\n?? Formalization/Legacy.lean\n?? Formalization/Manuscript.lean\n?? Formalization/Manuscript/\n?? PLAN.md\n?? aristotle_responses/\n?? aristotle_tasks/P17-finite-stabilizer-product-state.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P18-finite-coordinate-factorization.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P19-cstar-gns-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P20-finite-stabilizer-projector-expectation.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P21-one-qubit-positive-gns-data.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P22-finite-product-gns.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P23-infinite-algebraic-regional-equivalence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P24-infinite-algebraic-state-transport.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P25-cstar-completion-alpha-interface.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P26-cstar-alpha-gns-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P27-normal-von-neumann-extension-interface.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P28-product-factor-trace-dichotomy.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P29-finite-adapted-coordinate-star-equivalence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P30-finite-coordinate-equivalence-coherence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P31-constructed-algebraic-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P32-finite-product-state-coherence.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P33-cstar-inductive-limit-feasibility.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P34-finite-map-norm-control.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P35-concrete-cstar-completion.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P36-bicommutant-von-neumann-core.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P39-state-preserving-gns-model.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P40-bicommutant-normal-transport.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P41-product-factor-classification-boundary.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P42-regional-theorem-contract-audit.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P43-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P44-regional-product-state-and-cstar-model.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P45-spatial-gns-tensor-transport.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P46-local-hyperbolic-tensor-decomposition.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P47-center-finite-projection-core.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P49C-kaplansky-density.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P54-uhf-reference-representation.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P56-regional-product-state-identity.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P59-local-hyperbolic-factor-trace-theorem.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P61-hyperbolic-implies-central-criterion.md\n?? reviews/\n?? work/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && printf '\\\\n--- PLAN P54 ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 12 'P54|P52|P53|P55|Lane H|UHF' PLAN.md && printf '\\\\n--- DECISION ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,300p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,360p' aristotle_tasks/P54-uhf-reference-representation.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && printf '\\\\n--- PLAN P54 ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 12 'P54|P52|P53|P55|Lane H|UHF' PLAN.md && printf '\\\\n--- DECISION ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,300p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && printf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,360p' aristotle_tasks/P54-uhf-reference-representation.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n\n--- PLAN P54 ---\n15-local-code projection tower, its strong limit `q`, and the finite corner\n16-`q M_Gamma q`. Prove that the vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal\n17-tracial **state** on that corner, hence that `q` is finite; prove `q` is full;\n18-and derive that every nonzero central projection `z` has `zq != 0` finite in\n19-`z M_Gamma`. Conclude that no nonzero central summand is type III.\n20-\n21-This lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\n22-trace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\n23-separate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\n24-of a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\n25-merely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n26-\n27:### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n28-\n29-**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n30-\n31-From a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\n32-their coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\n33-models, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\n34-the special regional algebra is spatially isomorphic to\n35-\n36-`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed`.\n37-\n38-After proving the two factors and their spatial tensor product, derive the\n39-trivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\n40-not follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\n41-spatial factorization.\n42-\n43-### Reconnection\n44-\n45:Lane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\n46-concrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\n47-the general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\n48-that the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\n49-the two results remain logically independent.\n50-\n51-## Aristotle package sequence\n52-\n53-### Shared/central core\n54-\n55-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n56-|---|---|---|\n57-| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n58-| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n59-| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n60-| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n61-| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n62-| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n63-| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, then prove normality and faithfulness from the exact vector-functional and density/commutation hypotheses used in the manuscript. |\n64-| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n65-\n66-### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n67-\n68-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n69-|---|---|---|\n70:| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n71:| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n72:| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n73:| P55 | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Construct source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras and extend the P53 alpha by density. |\n74-| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Prove the stabilizer/product-state equality on finite Pauli words and extend it by density and continuity. |\n75-| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n76:| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n77-| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n78-\n79-### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n80-\n81-| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n82-|---|---|---|\n83-| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Optional globalization of a full finite corner to a faithful normal semifinite weight, if needed beyond no-type-III exclusion. |\n84-| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n85-\n86-## Initial parallel wave\n87-\n88:Submit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\n89:and P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\n90-packets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\n91-they are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n92-\n93-## Non-negotiable gates\n94-\n95-1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n96-   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n97-2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n98-   theorem alone.\n99-3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n100-   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n101-4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n\n--- DECISION ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\n--- PACKET ---\n# P54 — faithful UHF reference representation\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** construct a reusable compatible representation of\n  the dyadic algebra; this packet makes no manuscript claim.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P54`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** none.\n- **Gate discharged:** provide a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator\n  representation from finite dyadic stages.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no assumed infinite tensor-product Hilbert\n  space, regional alpha, state identity, spatial tensor product, factor type,\n  or trace/weight classification.\n\nRead `PLAN.md` and `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md` before editing.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean`. Starting\nfrom the checked dyadic finite-stage system, construct compatible finite-stage\nHilbert-space/operator representations and a faithful representation of the\nalgebraic limit, or the strongest concrete pre-C-star representation supported\nby pinned Mathlib. Do not postulate an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\nIf completion of the algebraic representation requires an unavailable API,\nstate exactly the minimal isometric-representation interface and prove all\nfinite-stage compatibility and faithfulness facts below that boundary.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList any completion, boundedness, isometry, or faithfulness premise that cannot\nbe constructed. Do not conceal it in typeclass inference.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean`. Reuse\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`,\n`AristotleCandidates.AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation`, and\n`AristotleCandidates.ConcreteCStarCompletion` as appropriate.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation` succeeds.\n- The response separates constructed finite-stage/limit data from any supplied\n  completion interface.\n- No placeholder, forbidden declaration, or infinite-tensor-product assumption\n  is introduced.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
