{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p aristotle_responses/P54-extracted && tar -xzf aristotle_responses/P54-uhf-reference-representation.tar.gz -C aristotle_responses/P54-extracted --no-same-owner --no-same-permissions && candidate='aristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean'; sha256sum \\\"\"'$candidate\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- SUMMARY ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,300p' \\\"\"'${candidate%/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean}/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- CANDIDATE ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,460p' \\\"\"'$candidate\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- FORBIDDEN SCAN ---\\\\n'; rg -n -i 'sorry|admit|axiom|opaque|unsafe|implemented_by|native_decide|infinite tensor|barTensor|factor|trace|weight|regional|alpha' \\\"\"'$candidate\" || true'","aggregated_output":"786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9  aristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean\n\n--- SUMMARY ---\n# Summary of changes for run 5d753dc2-3d6a-4b24-96a8-82af541fb8cb\nPacket **P54 — faithful UHF reference representation** (Lane H, no predecessors) is complete. The single new file `AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` (~905 lines) builds cleanly (`lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation`, whole project also builds), contains no `sorry`/`admit`/`axiom`/`opaque`/`unsafe`, and every result checks with only the standard axioms `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.\n\n**Context: infrastructure only.** No manuscript claim is made. In particular no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is postulated, and no regional alpha, state identity, spatial tensor product, von Neumann factor type, or trace/weight classification is asserted.\n\n**Constructed data (everything below is built, nothing is assumed):**\n1. *Algebraic positive cone.* `sumSqCone` (additive submonoid generated by `star s * s`) for `*`-semirings, with induction, conjugation stability, star-alg-hom image, and the subtraction-free order `SumSqLE a b := ∃ p ∈ sumSqCone A, b = a + p` (reflexive, transitive, additive, closed under `nsmul`, with a parallelogram bound). This replaces the C*-positive cone, which is unavailable at this purely algebraic stage.\n2. *Finite-stage operator bound.* `matrix_two_exists_bound` and hence `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`: every element of a finite dyadic stage satisfies `star x * x ≼ c` with an explicit cone certificate, proved by induction along the matrix tower with no analytic input; extended to the limit as `qubitUHF_exists_bound`.\n3. *Trace facts.* `qubitTensorTrace_star`, `qubitTensorTrace_faithful`, `qubitUHFTrace_star`, `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`, `qubitUHFTrace_nonneg_of_mem_sumSqCone`.\n4. *GNS Hilbert space.* `uhfNormSq`, the key bound `uhfNormSq_mul_le` (algebraic substitute for `‖zw‖₂ ≤ ‖z‖ ‖w‖₂`), the pre-Hilbert space `UHFL2` and its completion `UHFGNS`. This is the trace-GNS completion of the algebraic limit — explicitly *not* an infinite tensor product.\n5. *Reference representation.* `uhfRep : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)` by left multiplication, **faithful** (`uhfRep_injective`), with unit cyclic vector (`uhfCyclicVector_norm = 1`) and vector-state identity `uhfRep_vector_state : ⟪Ω, uhfRep z Ω⟫ = τ z`.\n6. *Compatible finite stages.* `uhfStageRep`, `uhfStageRep_compat`, `uhfStageRep_injective`, the instantiated data `uhfRepData : QubitOperatorRepresentationData UHFGNS`, with `uhfRepData_rho_injective`, `uhfRepData_limitRep = uhfRep` and `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`.\n7. *Concrete pre-C\\*-model.* `UHFConcreteCStar := uhfRep.range.topologicalClosure` with its `CStarAlgebra` instance, the injective dense-range embedding `uhfConcreteEmbedding`, and minimality `uhfConcreteCStar_le`.\n\n**Supplied interfaces / auxiliary assumptions: none.** No completion, boundedness, isometry, or faithfulness premise had to be assumed; the boundedness of left multiplication is derived from the constructed algebraic cone bound, and the Hilbert space from Mathlib's uniform-space completion. The previously conditional finite-stage representation interface is now instantiated by constructed data rather than hypothesized.\n\n**Open obstruction:** none blocking this packet. The only design constraint worth recording is that the finite dyadic stages carry no additive-inverse structure at the ambient level, so the order theory was developed subtraction-free (ring structure is introduced only locally inside proofs).\n\nThe Properties table lists the 16 user-facing declarations: all 10 properties are marked `proved`, and the 6 definitions remain `in_progress`, as definitions do. All work is committed and pushed.\n--- CANDIDATE ---\nimport Formalization.DyadicTensorTower\nimport AristotleCandidates.AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation\nimport AristotleCandidates.ConcreteCStarCompletion\n\n/-!\n# A faithful reference representation of the dyadic (UHF) algebra\n\n**Context declaration.** *Infrastructure only*: this module makes no manuscript\nclaim.  It constructs reusable Lean mathematics.\n\nStarting from the checked dyadic finite-stage system\n`StabilizerHyperfinite.QubitTensorPower` / `qubitTensorPowerMap` of\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower` and its canonical normalized finite-stage\ntraces, this file **constructs**\n\n* the algebraic positive cone `sumSqCone` of finite sums of elements\n  `star s * s` in a `*`-ring, and the induced algebraic order `SumSqLE`;\n* the finite-stage operator bound `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`: for every\n  finite dyadic stage element `x` there are `c ≥ 0` and an explicit cone\n  certificate for `star x * x ≼ c • 1`, and its direct-limit form\n  `qubitUHF_exists_bound`.  These are proved *algebraically*, by induction\n  along the matrix tower; no C*-norm, functional calculus or completion is\n  used;\n* faithfulness `qubitTensorTrace_faithful` and hermitianity\n  `qubitTensorTrace_star` of the finite-stage normalized traces, and their\n  direct-limit counterparts;\n* the **GNS pre-Hilbert space** `UHFL2` of the algebraic limit\n  `QubitUHFAlgebra` for the canonical trace `qubitUHFTrace`, i.e. the algebraic\n  limit equipped with the inner product `⟪a, b⟫ = τ (star a * b)`;\n* its Hilbert-space completion `UHFGNS := UniformSpace.Completion UHFL2`\n  (a genuine `NormedAddCommGroup` + `InnerProductSpace ℂ` + `CompleteSpace`);\n* the trace-square-norm bound `uhfNormSq_mul_le` for left multiplication, the\n  purely algebraic substitute for the C*-inequality `‖z w‖₂ ≤ ‖z‖ ‖w‖₂`;\n* the representation `uhfRep : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)`\n  by left multiplication, its **faithfulness** `uhfRep_injective`, its unit\n  cyclic vector (`uhfCyclicVector_norm`), and the vector-state identity\n  `uhfRep_vector_state : ⟪Ω, uhfRep z Ω⟫ = τ z`;\n* the compatible family of finite-stage representations\n  `uhfRepData : QubitOperatorRepresentationData UHFGNS`, each stage\n  representation being injective (`uhfRepData_rho_injective`), whose induced\n  limit representation is `uhfRep` (`uhfRepData_limitRep`);\n* the concrete C*-algebra `UHFConcreteCStar`, the closure of the operator range\n  of `uhfRep` inside `UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS`, together with the dense range of the\n  canonical map from the algebraic limit.\n\n## What is supplied and what is constructed\n\nEverything above is **constructed** from the dyadic tower and its traces.  In\nparticular the Hilbert space is *not* supplied: it is the trace-GNS completion\nof the algebraic limit.  **No infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is\npostulated**, no von Neumann algebra, bicommutant, weak closure, tensor\nfactorization, factor type, trace or weight classification is claimed, and no\nmanuscript statement is used or asserted.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nNone.  All statements below are unconditional consequences of the pinned\nMathlib version and of the previously checked dyadic tower.\n-/\n\nnamespace StabilizerHyperfinite\n\nset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 1000000\nset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n\nopen scoped ComplexOrder InnerProductSpace\nopen Complex UniformSpace\n\n/-! ## 1. The algebraic sum-of-squares cone -/\n\nsection Cone\n\nvariable {A : Type*} [Semiring A] [StarRing A]\n\n/-- The algebraic positive cone of a `*`-semiring: the additive submonoid\ngenerated by the elements `star s * s`.  This is the purely algebraic\nsubstitute for the positive cone of a C*-algebra; no norm, order structure or\nfunctional calculus is involved. -/\ndef sumSqCone (A : Type*) [Semiring A] [StarRing A] : AddSubmonoid A :=\n  AddSubmonoid.closure (Set.range fun s : A => star s * s)\n\ntheorem star_mul_self_mem_sumSqCone (s : A) : star s * s ∈ sumSqCone A :=\n  AddSubmonoid.subset_closure ⟨s, rfl⟩\n\ntheorem zero_mem_sumSqCone : (0 : A) ∈ sumSqCone A := (sumSqCone A).zero_mem\n\ntheorem add_mem_sumSqCone {a b : A} (ha : a ∈ sumSqCone A) (hb : b ∈ sumSqCone A) :\n    a + b ∈ sumSqCone A := (sumSqCone A).add_mem ha hb\n\ntheorem nsmul_mem_sumSqCone {a : A} (ha : a ∈ sumSqCone A) (k : ℕ) :\n    k • a ∈ sumSqCone A := AddSubmonoid.nsmul_mem _ ha k\n\n/-- Induction principle for membership in the algebraic positive cone. -/\ntheorem sumSqCone_induction {p : A → Prop}\n    (hzero : p 0) (hgen : ∀ s : A, p (star s * s))\n    (hadd : ∀ x y, p x → p y → p (x + y)) {a : A} (ha : a ∈ sumSqCone A) : p a := by\n  refine AddSubmonoid.closure_induction (motive := fun x _ => p x) ?_ hzero\n    (fun x y _ _ => hadd x y) ha\n  rintro x ⟨s, rfl⟩\n  exact hgen s\n\n/-- The algebraic positive cone is stable under conjugation `a ↦ star v * a * v`. -/\ntheorem sumSqCone_conj {a : A} (ha : a ∈ sumSqCone A) (v : A) :\n    star v * a * v ∈ sumSqCone A := by\n  refine sumSqCone_induction (p := fun a => star v * a * v ∈ sumSqCone A) ?_ ?_ ?_ ha\n  · simp\n  · intro s\n    have h : star v * (star s * s) * v = star (s * v) * (s * v) := by\n      simp [star_mul, mul_assoc]\n    rw [h]\n    exact star_mul_self_mem_sumSqCone _\n  · intro x y hx hy\n    have h : star v * (x + y) * v = star v * x * v + star v * y * v := by\n      simp [mul_add, add_mul]\n    rw [h]\n    exact add_mem_sumSqCone hx hy\n\n/-- Star-algebra homomorphisms map the algebraic positive cone into the\nalgebraic positive cone. -/\ntheorem sumSqCone_map {B : Type*} [Semiring B] [StarRing B] [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℂ B]\n    (φ : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B) {a : A} (ha : a ∈ sumSqCone A) : φ a ∈ sumSqCone B := by\n  refine sumSqCone_induction (p := fun a => φ a ∈ sumSqCone B) ?_ ?_ ?_ ha\n  · simp\n  · intro s\n    rw [map_mul, map_star]\n    exact star_mul_self_mem_sumSqCone _\n  · intro x y hx hy\n    rw [map_add]\n    exact add_mem_sumSqCone hx hy\n\n/-- The algebraic order attached to the sum-of-squares cone, in a\nsubtraction-free formulation: `SumSqLE a b` means that `b` exceeds `a` by an\nelement of the algebraic positive cone.  Stating it this way makes it\nmeaningful for `*`-semirings, and in particular independent of which additive\ninverse structure a given stage algebra is equipped with. -/\ndef SumSqLE (a b : A) : Prop := ∃ p ∈ sumSqCone A, b = a + p\n\ntheorem SumSqLE.refl (a : A) : SumSqLE a a :=\n  ⟨0, zero_mem_sumSqCone, by simp⟩\n\ntheorem SumSqLE.trans {a b c : A} (hab : SumSqLE a b) (hbc : SumSqLE b c) : SumSqLE a c := by\n  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpEq⟩ := hab\n  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqEq⟩ := hbc\n  refine ⟨p + q, add_mem_sumSqCone hp hq, ?_⟩\n  rw [hqEq, hpEq, add_assoc]\n\ntheorem SumSqLE.add {a b a' b' : A} (h : SumSqLE a b) (h' : SumSqLE a' b') :\n    SumSqLE (a + a') (b + b') := by\n  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpEq⟩ := h\n  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqEq⟩ := h'\n  refine ⟨p + q, add_mem_sumSqCone hp hq, ?_⟩\n  rw [hpEq, hqEq]\n  abel\n\ntheorem SumSqLE.nsmul {a b : A} (h : SumSqLE a b) (k : ℕ) : SumSqLE (k • a) (k • b) := by\n  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpEq⟩ := h\n  refine ⟨k • p, nsmul_mem_sumSqCone hp k, ?_⟩\n  rw [hpEq, smul_add]\n\n/-- The two-term parallelogram bound\n`star (a+b) * (a+b) ≼ 2 • star a * a + 2 • star b * b`, witnessed by the\nexplicit cone element `star (a-b) * (a-b)`. -/\ntheorem SumSqLE.star_add_mul_self {A : Type*} [Ring A] [StarRing A] (a b : A) :\n    SumSqLE (star (a + b) * (a + b)) ((2 : ℕ) • (star a * a) + (2 : ℕ) • (star b * b)) := by\n  refine ⟨star (a - b) * (a - b), star_mul_self_mem_sumSqCone _, ?_⟩\n  simp only [star_add, star_sub, two_nsmul]\n  noncomm_ring\n\nend Cone\n\n/-! ## 2. The algebraic operator bound along the matrix tower -/\n\nsection MatrixBound\n\nopen Matrix\n\nvariable {B : Type*} [Semiring B] [StarRing B] [Algebra ℂ B] [StarModule ℂ B]\n\n/-- A nonnegative real scalar lies in the algebraic positive cone. -/\ntheorem algebraMap_mem_sumSqCone {c : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ c) :\n    algebraMap ℂ B (c : ℂ) ∈ sumSqCone B := by\n  have h : algebraMap ℂ B (c : ℂ)\n      = star (algebraMap ℂ B ((Real.sqrt c : ℝ) : ℂ)) *\n          algebraMap ℂ B ((Real.sqrt c : ℝ) : ℂ) := by\n    rw [← algebraMap_star_comm, ← map_mul, Complex.star_def, Complex.conj_ofReal,\n      ← Complex.ofReal_mul, Real.mul_self_sqrt hc]\n  rw [h]\n  exact star_mul_self_mem_sumSqCone _\n\nomit [StarRing B] [StarModule ℂ B] in\n/-- Natural-number multiples of scalars are scalars. -/\ntheorem nsmul_algebraMap (k : ℕ) (z : ℂ) :\n    k • algebraMap ℂ B z = algebraMap ℂ B ((k : ℂ) * z) := by\n  rw [map_mul, map_natCast, nsmul_eq_mul]\n\nvariable {n : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n]\n\nomit [Algebra ℂ B] [StarModule ℂ B] in\n/-- The star-square of a matrix unit is a diagonal matrix unit. -/\ntheorem star_single_mul_single (i j : n) (b : B) :\n    star (Matrix.single i j b) * Matrix.single i j b = Matrix.single j j (star b * b) := by\n  ext k l\n  simp only [Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.star_apply, Matrix.single_apply, ite_and]\n  aesop\n\nomit [Algebra ℂ B] [StarModule ℂ B] in\n/-- Diagonal matrix units of cone elements lie in the cone. -/\ntheorem single_diag_mem_sumSqCone {w : B} (hw : w ∈ sumSqCone B) (j : n) :\n    Matrix.single j j w ∈ sumSqCone (Matrix n n B) := by\n  refine sumSqCone_induction (p := fun w => Matrix.single j j w ∈ sumSqCone (Matrix n n B))\n    ?_ ?_ ?_ hw\n  · simp\n  · intro s\n    rw [← star_single_mul_single j j s]\n    exact star_mul_self_mem_sumSqCone _\n  · intro x y hx hy\n    rw [Matrix.single_add]\n    exact add_mem_sumSqCone hx hy\n\nomit [StarRing B] [StarModule ℂ B] in\n/-- Scalars in a matrix algebra are the sum of the diagonal matrix units. -/\ntheorem algebraMap_matrix_eq_sum_single (c : ℂ) :\n    algebraMap ℂ (Matrix n n B) c = ∑ i : n, Matrix.single i i (algebraMap ℂ B c) := by\n  rw [Matrix.algebraMap_eq_diagonal]\n  ext k l\n  rw [Matrix.sum_apply]\n  by_cases h : k = l\n  · subst h; simp [Matrix.single_apply]\n  · rw [Matrix.diagonal_apply_ne _ h]\n    refine (Finset.sum_eq_zero ?_).symm\n    intro x _\n    rw [Matrix.single_apply, if_neg]\n    rintro ⟨rfl, rfl⟩\n    exact h rfl\n\n/-- A coefficient bound lifts to a bound for the corresponding diagonal matrix\nunit. -/\ntheorem SumSqLE.single_diag {w : B} {c : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ c)\n    (h : SumSqLE w (algebraMap ℂ B (c : ℂ))) (j : n) :\n    SumSqLE (Matrix.single j j w) (algebraMap ℂ (Matrix n n B) (c : ℂ)) := by\n  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpEq⟩ := h\n  refine ⟨Matrix.single j j p +\n      ∑ i ∈ Finset.univ.erase j, Matrix.single i i (algebraMap ℂ B (c : ℂ)),\n    add_mem_sumSqCone (single_diag_mem_sumSqCone hp j) (AddSubmonoid.sum_mem _ ?_), ?_⟩\n  · intro i _\n    exact single_diag_mem_sumSqCone (algebraMap_mem_sumSqCone hc) i\n  · rw [algebraMap_matrix_eq_sum_single, ← Finset.add_sum_erase _ _ (Finset.mem_univ j), hpEq,\n      Matrix.single_add, add_assoc]\n\n/-- **Matrix induction step.**  If every coefficient of a `*`-algebra `B`\nadmits an algebraic scalar bound for its star-square, then so does every\nelement of the `2 × 2` matrix algebra over `B`.  The proof is purely\nalgebraic: matrix-unit decomposition plus the parallelogram bound.  No norm,\ncompletion or functional calculus is used. -/\ntheorem matrix_two_exists_bound {B : Type*} [Ring B] [StarRing B] [Algebra ℂ B] [StarModule ℂ B]\n    (hB : ∀ b : B, ∃ c : ℝ, 0 ≤ c ∧ SumSqLE (star b * b) (algebraMap ℂ B (c : ℂ)))\n    (X : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) :\n    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 ≤ c ∧\n      SumSqLE (star X * X) (algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c : ℂ)) := by\n  obtain ⟨c00, hc00, k00⟩ := hB (X 0 0)\n  obtain ⟨c01, hc01, k01⟩ := hB (X 0 1)\n  obtain ⟨c10, hc10, k10⟩ := hB (X 1 0)\n  obtain ⟨c11, hc11, k11⟩ := hB (X 1 1)\n  set P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B := Matrix.single 0 0 (X 0 0) with hP\n  set Q : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B := Matrix.single 0 1 (X 0 1) with hQ\n  set R : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B := Matrix.single 1 0 (X 1 0) with hR\n  set S : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B := Matrix.single 1 1 (X 1 1) with hS\n  have hX : X = (P + Q) + (R + S) := by\n    ext i j\n    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>\n      simp [hP, hQ, hR, hS]\n  refine ⟨4 * c00 + 4 * c01 + 4 * c10 + 4 * c11, by positivity, ?_⟩\n  have step1 : SumSqLE (star X * X)\n      ((2 : ℕ) • (star (P + Q) * (P + Q)) + (2 : ℕ) • (star (R + S) * (R + S))) := by\n    rw [hX]\n    exact SumSqLE.star_add_mul_self _ _\n  have step2 : SumSqLE ((2 : ℕ) • (star (P + Q) * (P + Q)))\n      ((2 : ℕ) • ((2 : ℕ) • (star P * P) + (2 : ℕ) • (star Q * Q))) :=\n    (SumSqLE.star_add_mul_self P Q).nsmul 2\n  have step3 : SumSqLE ((2 : ℕ) • (star (R + S) * (R + S)))\n      ((2 : ℕ) • ((2 : ℕ) • (star R * R) + (2 : ℕ) • (star S * S))) :=\n    (SumSqLE.star_add_mul_self R S).nsmul 2\n  have step4 := step1.trans (step2.add step3)\n  have hPP : SumSqLE (star P * P)\n      (algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c00 : ℂ)) := by\n    rw [hP, star_single_mul_single]\n    exact SumSqLE.single_diag hc00 k00 0\n  have hQQ : SumSqLE (star Q * Q)\n      (algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c01 : ℂ)) := by\n    rw [hQ, star_single_mul_single]\n    exact SumSqLE.single_diag hc01 k01 1\n  have hRR : SumSqLE (star R * R)\n      (algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c10 : ℂ)) := by\n    rw [hR, star_single_mul_single]\n    exact SumSqLE.single_diag hc10 k10 0\n  have hSS : SumSqLE (star S * S)\n      (algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c11 : ℂ)) := by\n    rw [hS, star_single_mul_single]\n    exact SumSqLE.single_diag hc11 k11 1\n  have step5 := ((hPP.nsmul 2).add (hQQ.nsmul 2)).nsmul 2\n  have step6 := ((hRR.nsmul 2).add (hSS.nsmul 2)).nsmul 2\n  have step7 := step4.trans (step5.add step6)\n  have hval :\n      (2 : ℕ) • ((2 : ℕ) • algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c00 : ℂ) +\n          (2 : ℕ) • algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c01 : ℂ)) +\n        (2 : ℕ) • ((2 : ℕ) • algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c10 : ℂ) +\n          (2 : ℕ) • algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B) (c11 : ℂ))\n        = algebraMap ℂ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B)\n            (((4 * c00 + 4 * c01 + 4 * c10 + 4 * c11 : ℝ) : ℂ)) := by\n    simp only [nsmul_algebraMap, ← map_add]\n    congr 1\n    push_cast\n    ring\n  rwa [hval] at step7\n\nend MatrixBound\n\n/-! ## 3. The dyadic stages satisfy the algebraic operator bound -/\n\nsection DyadicBound\n\n/-- Every complex algebra whose additive structure is a semiring is in fact a\nring: the additive inverse is `(-1 : ℂ) • ·`.  The resulting `Ring` structure\nhas *the same* underlying `Semiring`, so it can be introduced locally in a\nproof without disturbing the ambient algebraic structure. -/\nnoncomputable def ringOfComplexAlgebra (A : Type*) [S : Semiring A] [Algebra ℂ A] : Ring A :=\n  letI : AddCommGroup A := Module.addCommMonoidToAddCommGroup ℂ\n  { S, (inferInstance : AddCommGroup A) with }\n\ntheorem ringOfComplexAlgebra_toSemiring (A : Type*) [S : Semiring A] [Algebra ℂ A] :\n    (ringOfComplexAlgebra A).toSemiring = S := rfl\n\n/-- The scalar stage: `star z * z` is the scalar `normSq z`. -/\ntheorem complex_exists_bound (z : ℂ) :\n    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 ≤ c ∧ SumSqLE (star z * z) (algebraMap ℂ ℂ (c : ℂ)) := by\n  refine ⟨Complex.normSq z, Complex.normSq_nonneg z, 0, zero_mem_sumSqCone, ?_⟩\n  simp [Complex.normSq_eq_conj_mul_self]\n\n/-- **Finite-stage algebraic operator bound.**  For every element `x` of a\nfinite dyadic stage there is a nonnegative real `c` with\n`star x * x ≼ c • 1` in the algebraic sum-of-squares order.  Proved by\ninduction along the matrix tower, with no analytic input. -/\ntheorem qubitTensorPower_exists_bound (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower n) :\n    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 ≤ c ∧ SumSqLE (star x * x) (algebraMap ℂ (QubitTensorPower n) (c : ℂ)) := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => exact complex_exists_bound x\n  | succ n ih =>\n    letI : Ring (QubitTensorPower n) := ringOfComplexAlgebra _\n    exact matrix_two_exists_bound (B := QubitTensorPower n) ih x\n\nend DyadicBound\n\n/-! ## 4. Hermitianity and faithfulness of the dyadic traces -/\n\nsection TraceProperties\n\n/-- The finite-stage normalized traces are hermitian. -/\ntheorem qubitTensorTrace_star (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower n) :\n    qubitTensorTrace n (star x) = star (qubitTensorTrace n x) := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero =>\n    show scalarTrace (star (x : ℂ)) = star (scalarTrace (x : ℂ))\n    rfl\n  | succ n ih =>\n    show normalizedMatrixTraceOver (Fin 2) (qubitTensorTrace n)\n        (star (x : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (QubitTensorPower n))) =\n      star (normalizedMatrixTraceOver (Fin 2) (qubitTensorTrace n) x)\n    rw [normalizedMatrixTraceOver_apply, normalizedMatrixTraceOver_apply]\n    have hentry : ∀ i : Fin 2,\n        qubitTensorTrace n ((star (x : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (QubitTensorPower n))) i i) =\n          star (qubitTensorTrace n (x i i)) := by\n      intro i\n      rw [Matrix.star_apply, ih]\n    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => hentry i]\n    simp [Fintype.card_fin]\n\n/-- Faithfulness at the scalar stage. -/\ntheorem complex_trace_faithful (z : ℂ) (hz : scalarTrace (star z * z) = 0) : z = 0 := by\n  have h : star z * z = 0 := hz\n  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h with h' | h'\n  · exact star_eq_zero.mp h'\n  · exact h'\n\n/-- The finite-stage normalized traces are faithful. -/\ntheorem qubitTensorTrace_faithful (n : ℕ) (x : QubitTensorPower n)\n    (hx : qubitTensorTrace n (star x * x) = 0) : x = 0 := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => exact complex_trace_faithful x hx\n  | succ n ih =>\n    set X : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (QubitTensorPower n) := x with hXdef\n    have hpos : ∀ i j : Fin 2, ∃ r : ℝ, 0 ≤ r ∧\n        qubitTensorTrace n (star (X j i) * X j i) = (r : ℂ) :=\n      fun i j => (qubitTensorTrace_isAlgebraicTracialState n).positive (X j i)\n    choose r hr_nonneg hr_val using hpos\n    have hsum : ((∑ i : Fin 2, ∑ j : Fin 2, r i j : ℝ) : ℂ) = 0 := by\n      have hx' : normalizedMatrixTraceOver (Fin 2) (qubitTensorTrace n) (star X * X) = 0 := hx\n      rw [normalizedMatrixTraceOver_apply] at hx'\n      have hmt : ∑ i : Fin 2, qubitTensorTrace n ((star X * X) i i)\n          = ∑ i : Fin 2, ∑ j : Fin 2, qubitTensorTrace n (star (X j i) * X j i) :=\n        matrixTraceOver_star_mul_self (Fin 2) (qubitTensorTrace n) X\n      rw [hmt] at hx'\n      have hne : (1 / (Fintype.card (Fin 2) : ℂ)) ≠ 0 := by\n        simp [Fintype.card_fin]\n      have hzero : ∑ i : Fin 2, ∑ j : Fin 2, qubitTensorTrace n (star (X j i) * X j i) = 0 :=\n        (mul_eq_zero.mp hx').resolve_left hne\n      rw [← hzero]\n      push_cast\n      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => (hr_val i j).symm\n    have hsumR : ∑ i : Fin 2, ∑ j : Fin 2, r i j = 0 := by exact_mod_cast hsum\n    have hall : ∀ i j : Fin 2, r i j = 0 := by\n      intro i j\n      have h1 : ∀ i ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 2)), 0 ≤ ∑ j : Fin 2, r i j :=\n        fun i _ => Finset.sum_nonneg fun j _ => hr_nonneg i j\n      have h2 : ∑ j : Fin 2, r i j = 0 :=\n        (Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg h1).mp hsumR i (Finset.mem_univ i)\n      exact (Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg\n        (fun j _ => hr_nonneg i j)).mp h2 j (Finset.mem_univ j)\n    have hentry : ∀ i j : Fin 2, X j i = 0 := by\n      intro i j\n